@@ -54,7 +54,9 @@ Normal Codex workers use native `on-request` approval with the `auto_review` rev
 
 Approved escalated commands execute outside the sandbox. The reviewer and task authorization govern those commands, including source writes during a no-source-edits review. This does not provide an OS-enforced read-only boundary for an approved command. Auto-review requires runtime and account support and can consume additional Codex usage. An explicit `--approval-mode never` retains noninteractive execution only when the task calls for approvals to be disabled. Required checks that then cannot run remain blocked. It is not a prerequisite or fallback for normal pstack work. Reviewed execution cannot be combined with `danger-full-access`. An explicitly authorized full-access task must also select `--approval-mode never`, which disables review rather than granting new task authority.
 
-The brief names the required UI assertions, screenshot outputs, tests, and authorized Git operations. The worker runs and interprets its own verification. On macOS, Chrome can abort during application registration inside the OS sandbox even in headless mode. For this known boundary, request review of the authorized browser command before launching it. Use a dedicated profile. Do not replace browser checks with static checks or move them to the coordinator. Preserve reviewer denials and unsupported requests as explicit capability gaps. Do not weaken tests, move Git metadata, or disable signing to avoid a denial. A no-source-edits review can still need temporary fixture outputs, sockets, or a browser. Specify those capabilities separately from permission to edit sources.
+The runner prepares the macOS command boundary before submitting a task, including exact-thread continuation. It checks the effective owned hook, trust, configuration and conflicting rewrites. Unsupported states fail before a task turn. Receiving runtime context is supplied automatically; the parent does not need to transcribe browser precautions. The worker still owns its UI assertions, screenshots and required tests.
+
+In a scoped macOS worker, a shell command selected for Seatbelt execution returns `PSTACK_REVIEW_REQUIRED` before the original command starts. Retry the same task-authorized operation through native reviewed escalation. This covers browser processes launched by Node, npm or test scripts without classifying command text. Use dedicated browser profiles and preserve denied checks as capability gaps. The guard changes no approval decision and grants no new task authority. Native hook errors or timeouts can fail open in the host, and specialized non-shell paths are outside this guardrail. Claude's own native Bash policy remains unchanged.
 
 Each independent seat and new round gets a unique run directory and fresh Codex thread. Use `--resume EXACT_THREAD_ID` only under poteto-mode's stateful-reuse exception. Never resume the latest thread or infer identity from a directory name. The runner uses the existing Codex CLI and authentication. Claude tools, MCP servers, conversation history, and permissions do not automatically become Codex tools or state. Verify the external executor has the capabilities needed for its assigned task.
 
